    "Mean reversion is strong in the final 7–10 days — model should be calibrated to gradually reduce forecast toward historical mean (last 10–15 days average) in the last 10 days of the horizon.",
    "Sentiment history is consistently neutral (0.00) — no sentiment-driven adjustment needed; model should not react to sentiment signals unless sentiment deviates from 0.00.",
    "Model underestimates prices in the final 5–7 days of the horizon — increase forecast by 1–3% for days 26–30 to account for potential rebound or lagged market reaction."
